loses stdin early (e.g., `head -c 1` on a large input) and verifies exit code 0\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The massive stitch task description for task #5114, implementing srd006-cat R5.4, with full project context, execution constitution, go style constitution, constraints, and acceptance criteria\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed conversation summary\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create cmd/cat/cat_test.go with differential test cases for R5.4 (and potentially other cat behaviors since the test file doesn't exist)\n   - Verify cmd/cat/main.go properly implements R5.4 (appears to already be done)\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/cat/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/cat/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I was in the research/planning phase of implementing task #5114. I had just finished reading all four relevant files:\n   - srd006-cat.yaml (R5.4 spec)\n   - cmd/cat/main.go (existing implementation - already has SIGPIPE handler)\n   - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (does not exist - needs creation)\n   - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (testing framework)\n   - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (SIGPIPE handler implementation)\n   \n   I had determined that R5.4 is already implemented in main.go and was about to create the test file.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Create cmd/cat/cat_test.go with differential test cases. The file needs to:\n   - Have the copyright header\n   - Import testing, os/exec, and pkg/testutils\n   - Use BuildBinary(t, \".\") to compile cat\n   - Use exec.LookPath(\"gcat\") with t.Skip\n   - Include DiffTest cases that exercise SIGPIPE behavior (R5.4) - e.g., piping large input through cat and having the downstream consumer close early\n   - Follow the shared_protocols differential testing pattern\n   - Then run `go build -o bin/cat ./cmd/cat/` and `go test ./cmd/cat/ -count=1` to verify acceptance criteria AC1-AC4\n\nIf you need specific details from before compact