{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018hsYXCGgR417qwwMmyd1AB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All done. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**R5.4 fix in `cmd/cat/main.go`**: Added EPIPE detection alongside the existing SIGPIPE handler. Go delivers SIGPIPE asynchronously via the handler goroutine, but the write returns EPIPE synchronously — creating a race where the main goroutine could exit 1 before the handler calls `os.Exit(0)`. The fix checks for EPIPE on write errors and exits 0 immediately, matching GNU behavior. Added `syscall` import and a 3-line check in the error handling path.\n\n**Created `cmd/cat/cat_test.go`** with:\n- `TestDiff` — 15 differential test cases against `gcat` covering stdin passthrough, binary data, line numbering (-n/-b), blank squeezing (-s), non-printing display (-v/-E/-T/-A/-e/-t/-u), and flag combinations\n- `TestDiffFiles` — multi-file concatenation with file fixtures\n- `TestMissingFile` — error handling for nonexistent files (exit 1, stderr message, remaining files processed)\n- `TestSIGPIPE` — R5.4 verification: pipes 1MB through cat, closes the read end after 1 byte, confirms exit 0"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":230,"cache_read_input_tokens":68810,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":230},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d5f60e36-e297-4b85-996a-784e4544a5df","uuid":"b49c5b51-d4a1-45d0-820c-4700669b7099"}
